---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CopyCommand from "../../components/CopyCommand.astro";
import { installCommand, repository } from "../../lib/catalog";
---

<Layout title="Getting started" active="start">
  <div class="wrap guide-page installation-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">A small addition to your workflow</p>
    <h1>
      Your next skill.
      <br />
      <em>Ready when you are.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Skills are plain Markdown instructions your agent can follow.
      <br />
      Install the ones you need, then put them to work.
    </p>
    <div class="guide-grid">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2 id="install">1. Choose and install</h2>
        <p>
          With Node.js and npm installed, open a terminal in your project and
          run:
        </p>
        <CopyCommand command={installCommand()} />
        <p>
          The installer lets you pick skills and choose which supported agents
          to install them for. Follow its prompts to select the installation
          scope.
        </p>
        <p>Already know the skill you want? Install just that one:</p>
        <CopyCommand command={installCommand("diagnose")} />
        <h2 id="invoke">2. Ask your agent to use it</h2>
        <p>Start with a real task and name the skill:</p>
        <CopyCommand
          command="Use the diagnose skill to investigate this failing test."
          label="Copy example prompt"
        />
        <p>
          Most skills can also load automatically when an agent recognizes a
          matching task. Some run only when you ask; others require a harness
          event. Every skill page explains its invocation mode.
        </p>
        <h2 id="adapt">3. Make the workflow yours</h2>
        <p>
          Read the installed SKILL.md. Keep the instructions that help, and
          adapt the workflow to your project. You can begin with one skill and
          add more as you need them.
        </p>
        <h2 id="manual">Prefer a manual install?</h2>
        <p>
          Copy the entire skill directory from the repository into your agent’s
          skills directory. Include bundled scripts, references, and assets when
          present. Check your agent’s documentation for its supported location.
        </p>
        <p>
          For Claude Code, a personal skill directory can live at{" "}
          <code>~/.claude/skills/&lt;skill-name&gt;/</code>. For a local
          checkout, this repository also includes{" "}
          <code>scripts/link-skills.sh</code>.
        </p>
        <section class="faq" aria-labelledby="questions">
          <h2 id="questions">Common questions</h2>
          <p class="faq-intro">A few useful answers before you get started.</p>
          <div class="faq-list">
            <details>
              <summary>Which agent can I use?</summary>
              <p>
                The skills installer supports agents including Claude Code,
                Codex, and Cursor. The instructions are portable Markdown, but
                individual skills may require additional tools. Read each
                skill’s instructions before using it.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Should I install every skill?</summary>
              <p>
                Start with a specific task. Install a skill for that task, learn
                its workflow, and expand your toolkit when it helps.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>What if my agent doesn’t find the skill?</summary>
              <p>
                Check that you installed it for the agent and scope you’re
                using. Start a new session if your agent requires it, then name
                the skill explicitly. Review the installer’s output for the
                destination directory.
              </p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>How is the repository licensed?</summary>
              <p>
                The repository uses the PolyForm Shield 1.0.0 license. Some
                skills include third-party material with separate attribution.
                Review the{" "}
                <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>license</a> and{" "}
                <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md`}>
                  third-party notices
                </a>
                .
              </p>
            </details>
          </div>
          <p class="faq-help">
            Still stuck?{" "}
            <a href={`${repository}/issues`}>Ask a question on GitHub</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
      <aside class="guide-aside" aria-label="Guide navigation">
        <p class="eyebrow">On this page</p>
        <a href="#install">Choose and install</a>
        <a href="#invoke">Use a skill</a>
        <a href="#adapt">Make it yours</a>
        <a href="#manual">Manual installation</a>
        <a href="#questions">Common questions</a>
        <hr />
        <p>Have a task in mind?</p>
        <a class="button" href="/#library">
          Find a skill →
        </a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .installation-page {
    max-width: 1100px;
    padding-block: 40px 56px;
  }
  .installation-page h1 {
    font-size: clamp(38px, 4.2vw, 58px);
    margin: 14px 0 18px;
  }
  .installation-page .lead {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .guide-grid {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 200px;
    gap: 40px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .prose > h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .guide-aside {
    margin-top: 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .faq {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }
  .faq h2 {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .faq .faq-intro {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  .faq-list {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--white);
  }
  .faq details {
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .faq details + details {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .faq summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    min-height: 58px;
    padding: 15px 20px;
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .faq summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .faq summary::after {
    content: "";
    flex: 0 0 18px;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 12px 1.5px
        no-repeat,
      linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 1.5px 12px
        no-repeat;
  }
  .faq details[open] summary::after {
    background: linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 12px
      1.5px no-repeat;
  }
  .faq summary:hover,
  .faq details[open] summary {
    background: #eef1e7;
  }
  .faq summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: -4px;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .faq details > p {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 14px 20px 20px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .faq .faq-help {
    font-size: 13px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    .installation-page {
      padding-block: 28px 40px;
    }
    .installation-page h1 {
      font-size: clamp(34px, 8vw, 46px);
    }
    .installation-page .lead {
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    .guide-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
      margin-top: 24px;
    }
    .guide-aside {
      grid-row: 1;
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 8px;
      padding: 0 0 18px;
      border-top: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .guide-aside .eyebrow {
      width: 100%;
    }
    .guide-aside > a:not(.button) {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 6px 10px;
      background: #eceee5;
      border-radius: 7px;
    }
    .guide-aside hr,
    .guide-aside > p:not(.eyebrow),
    .guide-aside .button {
      display: none;
    }
    .faq summary {
      padding-inline: 16px;
    }
    .faq details > p {
      padding-inline: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
